0 < 100 so all tier-one); rush? false so no rush charge; member? false so no discount; subtotal 185 < 250 so delivery charged", :rules "Progressive tiers: first 100 at $2, next 400 at $1.60, rest at $1.30. Rush adds 20% of production. Members get 10% of (production+rush) as discount capped at discount-cap; nonmembers get 0. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery fee $12 waived if subtotal-after-setup >= 250. Tax 8% on (subtotal+delivery). Round final total to cents half-up.", :operators "struct/slot for building and reading quote; + - * / for arithmetic; select for conditional branches (rush, member, delivery threshold); min/max for tier clamping and discount cap; round-money for final rounding; str for text output; network/define for constructing the pricing callable; pricing compound exposes numeric constants but is not a callable that computes a full quote", :outputs "A quote-1 struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total fields, a text reply to user-output-1, and a boolean test result to self-check-1", :operator "construct a network named compute-quote-1 that reads order-1 fields and pricing constants, computes the full breakdown, and writes into quote-1", :units "currency in dollars, copies as integers", :unknowns "none", :facts "quantity-1=80, rush-1=false, member-1=false, discount-cap-1=40, tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60M, tier-three-price=1.30M, rush-rate=0.20M, member-rate=0.10M, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08M", :decision :construct}, :selected-reference nil, :selected-callable false, :request-count 1, :identity {:id #uuid "08f05dce-2b43-46e1-9074-f95aa1867a74", :run-id #uuid "96fe62f5-41e1-4849-9ddf-ae3abe9eb365"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "8d990adb-1c61-35e5-9594-c663bb17ba0e"}} {:round 2, :record {:tests "Verify tier split: production equals 100*2 + 140*1.60 = 424. Verify rush equals production*0.20. Verify discount equals min((production+rush)*0.10, 40) and is capped at 40. Verify subtotal equals production+rush-discount+setup-fee. Verify delivery is 0 since subtotal >= 250. Verify tax equals (subtotal+delivery)*0.08. Verify total equals round-money(subtotal+delivery+tax). These checks expose errors in tier boundaries, discount capping, delivery threshold logic, and rounding placement.", :branches "240 copies spans tier-one (100) and tier-two (140), no tier-three. Rush is active. Member discount applies but is capped at 40. Subtotal after discount+setup likely exceeds 250 so delivery is waived.", :rules "Progressive tiers: first 100 at $2, next 400 at $1.60, remainder at $1.30. Rush adds 20% of production. Member discount is 10% of (production+rush), capped at discount-cap. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery waived if subtotal >= 250. Tax 8% on (subtotal+delivery). Final total rounded half-up to cents; intermediates unrounded.", :operators "compute-quote-1: general network [order pricing] implementing the full pricing pipeline, returns struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total. Suitable for any order struct with the required slots. No other pricing-specific callables exist.", :outputs "A quote struct for order-2 (240 copies, member, rush) with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total, a text reply to user-output-2, and a boolean test to self-check-2.", :operator "compute-quote-1", :units "USD, copies, rates as decimals", :unknowns "none", :facts "order-2 has :quantity 240, :rush? true, :member? true, :discount-cap 40. pricing has tier-one-limit 100, tier-one-price 2, tier-two-count 400, tier-two-price 1.60, tier-three-price 1.30, rush-rate 0.20, member-rate 0.10, setup-fee 25, delivery-fee 12, free-delivery-threshold 250, tax-rate 0.08. compute-quote-1 is a general network [order pricing] that implements the full pricing pipeline and returns a struct with all quote slots.", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "fec47ad1-db3e-3166-82e7-68e688cfa043"}, :selected-callable true, :request-count 3, :identity {:id #uuid "08f05dce-2b43-46e1-9074-f95aa1867a74", :run-id #uuid "96fe62f5-41e1-4849-9ddf-ae3abe9eb365"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "8d990adb-1c61-35e5-9594-c663bb17ba0e"}} {:round 3, :record {:tests "Check that production equals sum of tier products (100*2 + 400*1.60 + 220*1.30 = 1126). Check rush=0 since rush?=false. Check discount equals min(0.10*1126, 40)=40. Check subtotal equals production - discount + setup = 1111. Check delivery=0 since subtotal>=250. Check tax equals 0.08*subtotal. Check total equals round-money(subtotal+tax). These verify each rule branch independently rather than repeating the same arithmetic path.", :branches "Standard service (rush=false) so rush charge=0. Member (member?=true) so discount applies. 720 copies spans all three tiers. Subtotal after discount+setup will exceed free-delivery-threshold so delivery=0.", :rules "Progressive tiers: first 100 at $2, next 400 at $1.60, remainder at $1.30. Rush adds 20% of production. Member discount is 10% of (production+rush) capped at discount-cap. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery waived if subtotal>=250. Tax 8% on (subtotal+delivery). Final total rounded half-up to cents.", :operators "compute-quote-1: callable network [order pricing] -> struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total. Handles all tiers, rush, member discount with cap, setup, delivery threshold, tax, and rounding. Directly applicable to order-3 and pricing. No adaptation needed.", :outputs "A quote struct (production, rush, discount, subtotal, delivery, tax, total) connected to quote-3, a text summary connected to user-output-3, and a boolean check connected to self-check-3.", :operator "compute-quote-1", :units "USD, copies, rates as decimals", :unknowns "none", :facts "order-3 has quantity=720, rush?=false, member?=true, discount-cap=40. pricing has tier-one-limit=100