t-cap. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery waived if subtotal >= 250. Tax 8% on (subtotal+delivery). Final total rounded half-up to cents; intermediates unrounded.\" :branches \"240 copies spans tier-one (100) and tier-two (140), no tier-three. Rush is active. Member discount applies but is capped at 40. Subtotal after discount+setup likely exceeds 250 so delivery is waived.\" :operators \"compute-quote-1: general network [order pricing] implementing the full pricing pipeline, returns struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total. Suitable for any order struct with the required slots. No other pricing-specific callables exist.\" :operator \"compute-quote-1\" :decision :reuse :tests \"Verify tier split: production equals 100*2 + 140*1.60 = 424. Verify rush equals production*0.20. Verify discount equals min((production+rush)*0.10, 40) and is capped at 40. Verify subtotal equals production+rush-discount+setup-fee. Verify delivery is 0 since subtotal >= 250. Verify tax equals (subtotal+delivery)*0.08. Verify total equals round-money(subtotal+delivery+tax). These checks expose errors in tier boundaries, discount capping, delivery threshold logic, and rounding placement.\"}\n\n## role-cell\nWork carefully from the problem and available facts. Follow the strict procedure and the response format for the current phase. The implementation source is admitted into one persistent lexical child.\n\n## procedure-cell\nStrict procedure, used on its own in this experiment. ANALYSIS phase: Before constructing a solution, (1) ground the problem: identify requested outputs, supplied facts, unknowns, units, applicable rules and relevant branches; (2) inspect available bindings and earlier source for relevant callable operators, checking parameters, outputs, assumptions and dependencies rather than names alone; (3) choose an approach: use a suitable existing operator with the current inputs; if none fits, explain the gap and decide whether to adapt an operator or construct one with explicit parameters. Return a concise structured analysis and operator-selection record. Do not implement yet. IMPLEMENTATION phase: implement the recorded approach, using the current inputs. Test it against the original rules with checks capable of exposing a mistake; repeating the implementation arithmetic is not an independent check. Keep new callable operators available. This procedure does not prescribe task-specific formulas or which operator to create.\n\n## output-format-cell\nRead phase first. In analysis phase, return ONLY one EDN map, no Markdown or executable forms, with nonempty string fields :outputs :facts :unknowns :units :rules :branches :operators :operator :tests, plus :decision equal to :reuse, :adapt, or :construct. Use \"none\" for unknowns or operator when appropriate. :operators must summarize the candidates actually available and their suitability. :operator names the selected existing callable for reuse/adapt or proposed new callable for construct. :tests describes independent tests and what mistakes they could detect. The host checks record completeness and existence of selected reuse/adapt callables, not the correctness of your analysis. In implementation phase, analysis-record contains your unchanged analysis. Return executable Lain source only, without fences. Existing parent ports must be connected, not redefined. order-N and pricing are input structs; quote-N has :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total. Connect the computed breakdown to those slots, a text reply to user-output-N, and your test outcome to self-check-N. N is the current round. Use Lain operations on inputs, not precomputed answer constants. Only final total is rounded to cents.\n\n## context-cell\nOne worker and lexical child remain alive throughout the questions. Earlier definitions remain available in the binding directory. written-code and history contain actual prior source and user/reply messages. Return new forms for the current ask. You may construct test cases or consistency checks using the available operators and connect a boolean result to self-check-N. The parent supplies no quote formula or solved example.\n\n## language-cell\n(define name expression) binds a cell. (network [parameters] body) creates a callable. A network body can contain local define forms and return its final expression, including a struct. (struct :key value ...) constructs connected fields. Read a field with ((slot :key) object). Write an existing field with (-> computed-value ((slot :key) output-object)). + - * / min max >= <= = str and round-money are support-aware operations. (select condition then-value else-value) selects a branch. round-money rounds to two decimals, half up; use it only on the final amount. str builds text from connected values. Unknown inputs leave dependent computations unresolved. ttms-premise-closure attaches a premise to a callable; invocation carries it to results. Example: (define f (ttms-premise-closure (network [x] (+ x 2)) some-premise)). inspect:premises accepts (cell:reference binding). The struct operators and primitive documentation are capabilities, not prebuilt pricing solutions.\n\n## rules-cell\nFictional print-shop rules: progressive production pricing: first tier-one-limit copies at tier-one-price each; next tier-two-count copies at tier-two-price each; remaining copies at tier-three-price each. Rush service adds rush-rate times production cost. Members receive member-rate times production plus rush charges as discount, capped by the order discount-cap; nonmembers receive no discount. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery costs delivery-fee, waived when subtotal after discount and setup is at least free-delivery-threshold. Apply tax-rate to the entire amount including delivery. Final total includes tax and is rounded half up to cents; intermediate values are not rounded.\n\n## metadata-cell\npricing exposes the shared numeric rules. Every order-N contains independently supported :quantity, :rush? boolean, :member? boolean, :discount-cap, and :question premise. question premises identify the corresponding requested quote. shared-rule identifies the validity premise for the general pricing rules. Keep independent orders separate. A promotional discount-cap belongs only to the order carrying it. delivery-note is unrelated. Quote output slots are production cost, rush charge, discount amount, subtotal after setup, delivery charge, tax amount, and final rounded total. Future orders are unknown until asked.\n\n## ask\nQuote 240 copies for a member using rush service. Show the charges and final total.\n\n## written-code\n[\"\\n\\n(define compute-quote-1\\n  (network [order pricing]\\n    (define qty ((slot :quantity) order))\\n    (define rush? ((slot :rush?) order))\\n    (define member? ((slot :member?) order))\\n    (define cap ((slot :discount-cap) order))\\n    (define t1-limit ((slot :tier-one-limit) pricing))\\n    (define t1-price ((slot :tier-one-price) pricing))\\n    (define t2-count ((slot :tier-two-count) pricing))\\n    (define t2-price ((slot :tier-two-price) pricing))\\n    (define t3-price ((slot :tier-three-price) pricing))\\n    (define rush-rate ((slot :rush-rate) pricing))\\n    (define member-rate ((slot :member-rate) pricing))\\n    (define setup-fee ((slot :setup-fee) pricing))\\n    (define delivery-fee ((slot :delivery-fee) pricing))\\n    (define free-threshold ((slot :free-delivery-threshold) pricing))\\n    (define tax-rate ((slot :tax-rate) pricing))\\n    (define t1-copies (min qty t1-limit))\\n    (define t2-copies (min (max (- qty t1-limit) 0) t2-count))\\n    (define t3-copies (max (- qty t1-limit t2-count) 0))\\n    (define production (+ (* t1-copies t1-price) (* t2-copies t2-price) (* t3-copies t3-price)))\\n    (define rush-charge (select rush? (* production rush-rate) 0))\\n    (define raw-discount (select member? (* (+ production rush-charge) member-rate) 0))\\n    (define discount (min raw-discount cap))\\n    (define subtotal (+ production rush-charge (- discount) setup-fee))\\n    (define delivery (select (>= subtotal free-threshold) 0 delivery-fee))\\n    (define tax (* (+ subtotal delivery) tax-rate))\\n    (define total (round-money (+ subtotal delivery tax)))\\n    (struct :production production :rush rush-charge :discount discount :subtotal subtotal :delivery delivery :tax tax :total total)))\\n\\n(define result-1 (compute-quote-1 order-1 pricing))\\n\\n(-> ((slot :production) result-1) ((slot :production) quote-1))\\n(-> ((slot :rush) result-1) ((slot :rush) quote-1))\\n(-> ((slot :discount) result-1) ((slot :discount) quote-1))\\n(-> ((slot :subtotal) result-1) ((slot :subtotal) quote-1))\\n(-> ((slot :delivery) result-1) ((slot :delivery) quote-1))\\n(-> ((slot :tax) result-1) ((slot :tax) quote-1))\\n(-> ((slot :total) result-1) ((slot :total) quote-1))\\n\\n(-> (str \\\"Quote for \\\" ((slot :quantity) order-1) \\\" copies (standard, nonmember):\\\\n\\\"\\n         \\\"  Production: $\\\" ((slot :production) result-1) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n         \\\"  Rush: $\\\" ((slot :rush) result-1) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n         \\\"  Discount: $\\\" ((slot :discount) result-1) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n         \\\"  Subtotal (incl. setup): $\\\" ((slot :subtotal) result-1) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n         \\\"  Delivery: $\\\" ((slot :delivery) result-1) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n         \\\"  Tax (8%): $\\\" ((slot :tax) result-1) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n         \\\"  Total: $\\\" ((slot :total) result-1))\\n    user-output-1)\\n\\n(define check-1\\n  (and\\n    (and (<= ((slot :quantity) order-1) ((slot :tier-one-limit) pricing))\\n         (= ((slot :production) result-1) (* ((slot :quantity) order-1) ((slot :tier-one-price) pricing))))\\n    (and (= rush-1 false) (= ((slot :rush) result-1) 0))\\n    (and (= member-1 false) (= ((slot :discount) result-1) 0))\\n    (= ((slot :subtotal) result-1) (+ ((slot :production) result-1) ((slot :setup-fee) pricing)))\\n    (and (< ((slot :subtotal) result-1) ((slot :free-delivery-threshold) pricing))\\n         (= ((slot :delivery) result-1) ((slot :delivery-fee) pricing)))\\n    (= ((slot :tax) result-1) (* (+ ((slot :subtotal) result-1) ((slot :delivery) result-1)) ((slot :tax-rate) pricing)))\\n    (= ((slot :total) result-1) (round-money (+ ((slot :subtotal) result-1) ((slot :delivery) result-1) ((slot :tax) result-1))))))\\n\\n(-> check-1 self-check-1)\"]\n\n## history\n[{:role \"user\", :content \"Quote 80 copies for a nonmember using standard service. Show the charges and final total.\"} {:role \"user\", :content \"Quote 240 copies for a member using rush service. Show the charges and final total.\"}]\n\n## Binding directory\n- and [unknown]: unknown | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"e329ced3-23b1-309e-bd1d-1ce9c429e1a9\"}\n- check-1 [unknown]: unknown | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"0c18a0d6-1783-38ac-83e9-b6da08493c19\"}\n- compute-quote-1 [known]: callable; inspect the binding and language-introduction-cell | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"fec47ad1-db3e-3166-82e7-68e688cfa043\"}\n- result-1 [known]: compound; inspect its immediate slots | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"2ceca786-c7dc-30b5-ac6d-7df85aa440cb\"}\n- inspect:premises [known]: callable; inspect the binding and language-introduction-cell | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"f3cafb7e-9825-334a-9404-100d70bcc84b\"}\n- cell:reference [known]: callable; inspect the binding and language-introduction-cell | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"39f5f4e0-c623-379f-aa92-7b07399b86d2\"}\n- struct [known]: callable; inspect the binding and language-introduction-cell | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"9054fc34-0286-3d4c-8271-a11522b21fed\"}\n- slot [known]: callable; inspect the binding and language-introduction-cell | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"4dd2cd77-3bf6-30bd-9f86-486b3d81a234\"}\n- round-money [known]: callable; inspect 